.TH BAO 1 "2026-09-06" "NuCode" "LAN vault"
.SH NAME
bao \- OpenBao vault as deployed on the NuCode LAN
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bao
is the OpenBao command-line client, a static Go binary, version 2.6.2 on this box. This page documents OpenBao AS DEPLOYED on the NuCode LAN, not the full upstream CLI (for that run:
.BI bao \-h
, or see the OpenBao docs). The vault runs as a Docker container named
.B bao
from
.BR /data/NuCode/Bao ,
reachable at
.BR https://192.168.88.18:8200
on the LAN and loopback only, behind a self-signed certificate. Day to day you drive it through
.BR bao-kit (1) ,
which sets the address, the CA cert and the token for you; reach for raw
.B bao
only for things
.B bao-kit
does not wrap.
.SH DEPLOYMENT
.PP
The vault is a docker compose service named bao, defined in /data/NuCode/Bao/docker-compose.yml, image openbao/openbao:2.6.2.
.PP
Raft storage lives on a named docker volume, so recreating the container does not lose data.
.PP
The listener binds 0.0.0.0:8200 inside the container; the host publishes it on 127.0.0.1:8200 and 192.168.88.18:8200.
.PP
TLS is a self-signed cert; clients must trust tls/bao.crt (BAO_CACERT).
.PP
The audit device and the kv v2 engine at kv/ are enabled at init time.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every raw bao call needs these; bao-kit sets them.
.TP
.B BAO_ADDR
https://192.168.88.18:8200
.TP
.B BAO_CACERT
Path to tls/bao.crt, so the client trusts the self-signed cert.
.TP
.B BAO_TOKEN
The auth token; if unset, bao-kit loads the cached login from ~/.config/openbao/token.
.PP
The quickest way to set all three is:
.nf
eval "$(bao-kit env)"
.fi
.SH DAILY USE
.PP
The host sleeps at night and the vault seals on every boot, so the day starts sealed. The morning ritual is:
.nf
bao\-kit unseal
bao\-kit login
.fi
After that,
.B bao\-kit status
should show sealed: False and a valid token. Raw equivalents exist
(.BR bao operator unseal ,
.BR bao login ) but the kit is the path.
.SH COMMANDS YOU USE
This is the subset of the bao CLI used on this box; the full command set is in
.BR bao \-h .
.TP
.BI "bao status"
Seal and HA status.
.TP
.BI "bao operator unseal" " KEY"
Submit an unseal key share (bao\-kit unseal wraps this).
.TP
.BI "bao kv get \-mount=kv" " PATH"
Read a secret (prints it; mind the transcript).
.TP
.BI "bao kv put \-mount=kv" " PATH field=value"
Replace a secret (whole secret).
.TP
.BI "bao kv patch \-mount=kv" " PATH field=value"
Merge fields into a secret (this is what bao\-kit put uses).
.TP
.BI "bao token lookup" / "bao token create"
Inspect or mint tokens.
.TP
.BI "bao login \-method=userpass" " username=ziggy"
Authenticate.
.TP
.BI "bao unwrap" " TOKEN"
Unwrap a response\-wrapping token.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.BI "Connection refused on 8200 though docker ps shows the container Up: "
Docker started the container without installing the host port publish (docker inspect shows PortBindings set but NetworkSettings.Ports empty; nothing listens on host :8200). It follows iptables churn from the LAN NAT link. Fix: recreate, do not just restart: cd /data/NuCode/Bao && docker compose down && docker compose up \-d . The raft data is on the named volume, so nothing is lost. Verify with docker port bao (expect both 127.0.0.1:8200 and 192.168.88.18:8200).
.TP
.BI "Every call 403s right after login: "
A stale exported BAO_TOKEN is shadowing the fresh cached token. Fix: unset BAO_TOKEN before the command.
.TP
.BI "sealed: True after a reboot: "
Expected; run bao\-kit unseal .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /data/NuCode/Bao/docker-compose.yml
The compose service.
.TP
.B /data/NuCode/Bao/tls/bao.crt
The self-signed CA cert (BAO_CACERT).
.TP
.B /data/NuCode/Bao/config/
The OpenBao server config (declares the listener and the file audit device).
.TP
.B ~/.config/openbao/init.json
Unseal key and root token, mode 600.
.TP
.B ~/.config/openbao/token
Cached operator login, mode 600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BI bao-kit (1)
is the wrapper you use day to day.
.PP
The vault repo README at
.B /data/NuCode/Bao/README.md
is authoritative.
.PP
The full upstream CLI is in
.BI bao \-h
and the OpenBao documentation.
.PP
read this page without installing it:
.BI man ./docs/bao.1
